lexical.evidence_text:
Assignments are used to set values for registers.

Syntax: name=expression;

Where name is the name of the register, and expression is an arbitrary expression, which is evaluated and is set as a new value of the register.

Declarations are the first statements in the equation and are used to define the register in the equation and set its initial value.

Syntax: register name [= expression];

Where register is the key word, name is the name of the register, and expression (optional) is an arbitrary expression, which is evaluated and is set as the initial value of the register.
